olivia_acme: Hey team — trying to finish a POC with Redwood JS SDK. We're streaming chat + using tool calls to fetch customer records. Hitting two blockers: 1) structured output schema from tool calls doesn't match our consumer (they expect `customer.v1`), SDK returns `tool_response` wrapper. 2) pricing: need an estimate if we go reserved for pilot ~10 rps sustained, burst to 50. Also SSO/IP allowlist + KMS Qs from infra.

maria_sales: Thanks Olivia — we can do a 30m debug pairing. looping in Ajay for SDK/stream details and Pat for infra/KMS.

ajay_solutions: quick Qs: are you using streaming SSE or websocket? sample SDK call and a snippet of the tool output would help.

olivia_acme: using JS SDK streaming with `client.chat.stream(...)` and function calls. sample tool response pasted below — the consumer only wants a top-level `customer` object, not nested in `tool_response`.

olivia_acme: ```json
{
  "tool_response": {
    "name":"customer_lookup",
    "result": {
      "customer": {"id":"123","name":"Acme Corp"},
      "meta": {"queried_by":"agent"}
    }
  }
}
```

ajay_solutions: got it. two options: (A) map on consumer side (fast) (B) instruct Redwood to emit structured output directly by using `structured_output_v1: true` in the call params and set `tool_call_mode: 'pass_args'`. example: ```js
await client.chat.stream({
  model: 'redwood-rlhf-1',
  structured_output_v1: true,
  tool_call_mode: 'pass_args',
  tools: [lookupCustomerTool]
})
```

ajay_solutions: that will emit `{ "customer": {...} }` as the top-level structured payload. If you must keep current SDK path, we can add a tiny transform middleware in the SDK client to unwrap `tool_response.result.customer`.

pat_platform: KMS/infra notes: BYOK KMS is only available on Private and Dedicated with enterprise contracts. For a Hosted reserved pilot we can offer encrypted-at-rest keys managed by Redwood but integrate with your HSM via signed attestations. IP allowlist + SSO: we support IP allowlist for Dedicated and Private; for Hosted we can gate by org SSO and IP ranges if you sign an addendum.

angela_security: From security side we'll need completed sections of the questionnaire: SAML flow (SP-initiated), SCIM provisioning, data residency, encryption at rest/in transit. Also need PoC evidence of audit logs and access controls. I can share a short checklist.

maria_sales: pricing: for 10 rps sustained with expected token sizes ~800 tokens/request, our quick calc for hosted reserved: ~2.4M tokens/day. For pilot we usually recommend a small Dedicated bucket: 4x A100 equivalent reserved for peak 50 rps bursts. Ballpark monthly commit: $XXk — I'll ask pricing to produce a tailored PDF.

olivia_acme: ballpark is fine for now. Can you also confirm fallback behavior if reserved runs out? We need predictable degradation, not complete failures.

ajay_solutions: Redwood supports two-tier routing — reserved capacity first, then overflow to lightweight hosted variants with higher latency or to cached responses. You can set policy `fallback: 'graceful'` which returns last-known-good answer from prefix cache or reroutes to smaller model. Example config: ```yaml
policies:
  - name: pilot-route
    primary: dedicated-pool:acme-pilot
    fallback: hosted-small
    fallback_behavior: graceful
```

pat_platform: also enable `cache: prefix_kv` to reduce token consumption for repetitive queries. That will keep degradation acceptable.

maria_sales: Action items: 1) Ajay to run pairing session with Olivia tomorrow 10:00am PT (link: https://meet.redwood.internal/olivia-debug) 2) Pat to confirm KMS options and IP allowlist feasibility 3) Angela to send security checklist 4) Maria to get an initial pricing PDF from pricing team.

olivia_acme: +1 to all. pairing confirmed. For the SDK transform — if you can drop a tiny middleware snippet I can ship it to our backend quickly.

ajay_solutions: middleware snippet: ```js
client.on('tool_called', (msg) => {
  if (msg.tool_response && msg.tool_response.result && msg.tool_response.result.customer) {
    return msg.tool_response.result.customer;
  }
  return msg;
});
```

ajay_solutions: note: that is a stopgap; we'll test structured_output_v1 in the call so you can remove it later.

maria_sales: I'll open a presales ticket (#PS-4821) to track pricing/contract and add Olivia as watcher.

deploy-bot: deploy 2026-03-19 18:02 UTC: SDK patch v2.14.7 rolled to hosted — fixes streaming `tool_response` ordering.

pat_platform: FYI — the deploy includes a flag `structured_output_experiment` you can enable per-org if you want early access.

olivia_acme: perfect, thanks everyone. See you at 10am PT. :thumbsup:
